#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cross

#% text
# `cross(u, v)` gives the cross product of two vectors of length 3.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The result is perpendicular to `u` and `v`, with length `abs(u)*abs(v)*sin(angle)`; `cross(v, u)` is `-cross(u, v)`.

#% item
# Entries may be exact, symbolic or numerical.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cross([1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0])
#% output
#= [0, 0, 1]

#% cell
cross([1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6])
#% output
#= [-3, 6, -3]

#% cell
cross([a, b, c], [x, y, z])
#% output
#= [b*z - c*y, c*x - a*z, a*y - b*x]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The normal of the plane through three points:

#% cell
p = [1, 0, 0]; q = [0, 1, 0]; r = [0, 0, 1]; cross(q - p, r - p)
#% output
#= [1, 1, 1]

#% text
# The area of the triangle they span:

#% cell
norm(cross(q - p, r - p))/2
#% output
#= (1/2)*3^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The result is perpendicular to both factors:

#% cell
u = [1, 2, 3]; v = [-2, 0, 5]; [dot(u, cross(u, v)), dot(v, cross(u, v))]
#% output
#= [0, 0]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `dot`, `norm`, `curl`, `det`
